External programs this project only executes
--------------------------------------------
ghostdeck invokes the following programs when present. It does not
vendor, relicense, or redistribute them. Which lookup applies is stated
per entry.

Resolved on PATH (`shutil.which`, or a bare-name exec):

- adb (Android SDK platform-tools)
- ffmpeg
- ffprobe (ships with ffmpeg; `ghostdeck play` probes the source with it first)
- yt-dlp (optional; used only for URL sources)
- armv7-linux-gnueabihf-gcc (compiles the ARM device helpers)
- clang, xcrun, install_name_tool, codesign, ditto (Xcode command-line
  tools; build and sign the local hidshim Studio copy)
- ps (reads a process command line or start time to identify our own player, the
  virtual-HID keeper, and the Studio copy)
- pgrep, kill (used only by the opt-in hardware verification harness
  `tools/hardware_verify.py`: pgrep lists processes matching a pattern so the harness can
  find this repository's own local bridge, and kill sends a signal to an exact pid so it
  can stop the bridge process it started itself)
- ar, file (binutils and the file utility, when present; `device/build-color-agent.sh`
  inspects the libturbojpeg archive with them)

Invoked by absolute path:

- /bin/rm, /usr/bin/ditto (remove and copy the local Studio copy;
  ditto is also required on PATH as above)
- /usr/bin/open (launches the local Studio copy)

Programs the device helpers exec on the deck through adb (for example
/bin/sh, /bin/zkgui, and the staged proxy, preload, and agent) are not
host programs and are covered by the vendor-property note above.

Those programs keep their own licenses. Install them separately.
